            <ArticleTitle>Manual handling and nursing children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>36-42; quiz 43</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aim of this article is to highlight some of the unique challenges relating to handling children, such as: their stage of physical and cognitive development, their position in relation to the carer's centre of gravity, their level of comprehension and their ability to communicate.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
